C1 — LIKE / NOTIFICATION TRANSACTION BOUNDARY

Code trace (src/app/api/social/activities/[id]/like/route.ts):
  Line 75: await db.like.create({ ... })        ← uses db, NOT tx
  Line 99: await db.notification.create({ ... }) ← uses db, NOT tx
  
  These are TWO SEPARATE, non-transactional DB operations.
  No withTransaction() wrapper around them.
  
  Compare: connections/[id]/route.ts uses withTransaction(async (tx) => {...})
  with tx.auditLog.create inside the transaction.

Failure window:
  If db.notification.create throws a non-P2002 error (e.g. DB connection drop),
  the Like IS already persisted (line 75 committed) but the notification is LOST.
  
  The catch block (line 110-116) logs the error but does NOT roll back the Like.
  
  Resulting state:
    Like persisted = YES
    Notification expected = YES
    Notification missing = YES  ← atomicity gap

  The reverse (notification persisted, Like missing) is NOT possible because
  notification creation only happens if isNewLike === true (line 96), which
  means the Like was successfully created.

