C3 — CONNECTION RECIPROCAL INTEGRITY

Code trace:
  Schema: @@unique([followerId, followeeId]) on SocialConnection
    → Prevents duplicate rows in the same direction
    → Bidirectional friendship = 2 rows (A→B + B→A), both unique
  
  ACCEPT state machine (connections/[id]/route.ts:187):
    if (status === 'ACCEPTED' && conn.status !== 'PENDING') → 409 CONFLICT
    → Repeated ACCEPT on already-ACCEPTED connection returns 409
    → No duplicate rows created
  
  Authorization (line 165-180):
    ACCEPTED/REJECTED: only isFollowee can transition
    → A (follower) cannot self-accept → 403 NOT_FOLLOWEE
  
  Upsert on reverse edge (line 384-401):
    tx.socialConnection.upsert({
      where: { followerId_followeeId: { followerId: conn.followeeId, followeeId: conn.followerId } },
      create: { status: ACCEPTED, acceptedAt: now },
      update: { status: ACCEPTED, acceptedAt: now }
    })
    → Idempotent: if reverse edge exists, updates it; if not, creates it
    → Exactly 2 rows after accept (A→B + B→A), never more

