   produces exactly 2 rows. The @@unique constraint + state machine + upsert
   pattern makes duplicate/orphan edges impossible at the DB level.)

Classification: REJECT_FINDING
Reason: DB_CONSTRAINT_PREVENTS_DUPLICATES
  The @@unique([followerId, followeeId]) constraint prevents duplicate rows.
  The ACCEPT state machine (409 on non-PENDING) prevents repeated accept.
  The upsert on reverse edge prevents orphan/duplicate reciprocal rows.
  No code-level path produces >2 accepted rows or stale mixed states.

